---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import catalog from "../../catalog/releases.json";
const s=catalog.releases[0].summary;
---
<Base title="Documentation"><section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p><h1>From first transfer to reproducible analysis</h1><p>The structure is ready; public schemas and commands will replace these placeholders after release review.</p></section><section class="section docs"><nav><b>On this page</b><a href="#start">Getting started</a><a href="#access">Data access</a><a href="#formats">Formats</a><a href="#mapping">Mapping</a><a href="#citation">Citation</a></nav><article><section id="start"><p class="eyebrow dark">01</p><h2>Getting started</h2><p>Begin from an immutable release, model catalog, and small example bundle.</p><pre>python -m tigress_ncr_tools  # public example pending</pre></section><section id="access"><p class="eyebrow dark">02</p><h2>Data access</h2><p>Globus Web App and CLI instructions will include checksum verification and transfer sizes.</p></section><section id="formats"><p class="eyebrow dark">03</p><h2>Formats and schemas</h2><p>{s.formats}</p><p>{s.units} {s.numbering}</p><p>See the <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL+"releases/#summary"}>release data summary</a> for each product's cadence, format, and size.</p></section><section id="mapping"><p class="eyebrow dark">04</p><h2>Executed parameters</h2><p>The core catalog will report problem/zstar as run and distinguish the realized KG89 density from the original PHANGS coordinate.</p></section><section id="citation"><p class="eyebrow dark">05</p><h2>Citation</h2><p>The data are released under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a> licence (CC BY 4.0): reuse is open, with credit to the release paper. Example code and agent documentation are released under the BSD 3-Clause licence. The DOI, acknowledgment text, and support contact remain publication gates.</p></section></article></section></Base>
